        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 43.1b" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="569" ed="#liebermann"/>Pensandum tamen est, ut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Hn_43-1b.lnote.oe.13"/> ratione<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#Hn_43-1b.lnote.oe.c"/> et consideracione hoc fiat, ne fraudacionis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="d" target="#Hn_43-1b.lnote.oe.d"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Hn_43-1b.lnote.oe.14"/> pocius quam iuste repeticionis accio iudicetur.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 569 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
